## Phase 4 — Common failure modes & quick fixes

| Symptom                                          | Likely cause                                                 | Fix |
|--------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|-----|
| App crashes on launch with `frida -f`            | Jailbreak / Frida detection                                  | C.7 hooks; or `frida --runtime=v8`; or rename `frida-server` binary |
| `Failed to attach: unable to connect`            | `frida-server` not running or version mismatch               | `pkill frida-server; frida-server &`; pin host `frida-tools==frida-server` version |
| Burp shows no traffic, no errors in app          | CA installed but not trusted for TLS                         | Settings → About → Certificate Trust Settings → enable |
| `NSURLErrorDomain -1200`                         | TLS handshake fail — proxy CA missing OR pinning still on    | Verify CA in Safari first; then re-check bypass |
| Some requests proxied, others not                | App uses two HTTP stacks (e.g., NSURLSession + Alamofire)    | Layer hooks: C.1 + C.4 + C.5 as needed |
| Bypass works once, fails on re-launch            | App caches pin result in keychain / does a *background* re-pin | Hook `keychainServices` or rerun bypass with `--no-pause -f` each launch |
| Flutter app — nothing works                      | BoringSSL inside Flutter ignores system trust                | C.5 path, must hit Flutter's verify function |
| App is React Native / NativeScript               | JS-layer pinning sometimes via `react-native-ssl-pinning`    | Either Frida-hook the bridge call or patch the JS bundle |

